{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1285559-gods-and-monsters-errata-thread","id":1285559,"title":"Gods and Monsters errata thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-07T07:29:30-08:00","id":1285559,"title":"Gods and Monsters errata thread","content":"Please put your errata for <b>M20 Gods and Monsters</b> here.<br /> <br /> The usual rules apply. Stylistic opinions on whether we should use a semicolon instead of a comma aren't errata. Errata include things like missing words, cut-off sentences, art overlapping text, typos, and other obvious errors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:54:02-08:00","id":1285650,"title":"","content":"Some points I have noticed skimming through it include a p. xx reference in the second paragraph of page 185 (a quick search reveals many additional such p. xx references). Also, I noticed that on the page 5 heading for chapter 4, &quot;Ephemeral Entities&quot; lacks a space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4335-alassalaur","name":"Alassalaur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T15:55:45-08:00","id":1285709,"title":"","content":"P. XXs aren't being addressed until after errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T16:49:48-08:00","id":1285728,"title":"","content":"The Hedge Magician mentions taking four to ten Common Magickal Effects (from M20 pp.508\u2013510) if you don't have any books with Hedge Magic rules in them, but it didn't suggest what dice pool to use: Hedge Magicians don't have an Arete pool to roll. I suggest rolling whatever the highest Sphere rating for the Effect happens to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T17:11:27-08:00","id":1285736,"title":"","content":"pg 201 talks about getting innate armor but it says it can't soak aggravated unless you spend twice the points on it. Typically armor applies soak to all aggravated (pg 416 of M20), not sure if this was a misprint or not. If it is, I would suggest changing the terminology to soak instead of armor. <br /> <br /> pg 104 The stats for animals seem to be all over the place. A gorilla has 4 strength, yet they're about five times stronger than human in real world, they also only have 6 health levels as opposed to a human's 7 levels. A bear is on the opposite spectrum, having 6 strength and 10 health levels. An elephant is at 7 strength, just one above a bear, but also have 10 health levels. A great white is sitting at 6 strength and 9 health levels.<br /> I'd suggest giving entries ranges of recommended Attributes much like the Bygone Bestiary did for 2e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T19:10:52-08:00","id":1285766,"title":"","content":"pg. 40<br /> <br /> Jayleen knows he\u2019s touched by God.<br /> <br /> Should be Jayleen knows she's touched by God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T10:49:27-08:00","id":1285957,"title":"","content":"Page 79; Constructs; Artificial People; Darius<br /> <br /> The last sentence of the first full paragraph after the heading &quot;Darius&quot;. It reads &quot;[t]he ideal playmate for certain tastes, he\u2019s only good for only thing\u2026 but he\u2019s very good at that.&quot; I'm assuming that it should read &quot;he's only good for <b>one</b> thing....&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T21:44:39-08:00","id":1286093,"title":"","content":"Page 37:<br /> <br /> The name 'Kore Valkyrie Smith' should probably be 'Kore &quot;Valkyrie&quot; Smith.' (Based upon context, it sounds like Valkyrie is a nickname and not her actual middle name.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T09:00:45-08:00","id":1286202,"title":"","content":"I've seen a lot of people pointing out that the rules for severe Unbelief will basically kill anything dead in under a minute, making the rules meaningless for practical purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T18:29:13-08:00","id":1286336,"title":"","content":"Page 215:<br /> <br /> The Bargain Charm doesn't state the difficulty of the spirit's Gnosis+Willpower roll or the mage's opposing Willpower roll. It also doesn't state what the Charm actually <i>does</i> if the spirit uses it successfully.<br /> <br /> Is it supposed to affect the Contest of Wills (HDYDT p.94)? Most of the other steps in the bargaining process are pretty vague rules-wise already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:11:06-08:00","id":1286696,"title":"","content":"p. 4: &quot;The Fae&quot; sub-subheading should be the same margin as the rest of the Night-Folk (Vampires, Werebeasts and Ghosts). This makes it look like the Fae are a subset of Werebeasts. Similarly, the Fae aren't with the pdf bookmarks for the Night-Folk, but included in the Werebeasts one. On p. 70, the type for The Fae header isn't the same size as the rest of the Night-Folk ones. It looks like someone in layout thought the Fae are a kind of werecreature, but the text makes it clear that Faeries are very different form both vampires and werewolves.<br /> <br /> p. 5: Our Lady, the Merciful Mother 163 is in italics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T21:13:49-08:00","id":1286969,"title":"","content":"Page 18, the image should be lower, every other instance has the full horizontal line across a heading like this and the small rectangular image below it.<br /> Page 27: first paragraph under Brain &quot;they often to go Brain&quot; should be &quot;they often go to Brain&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T11:51:40-08:00","id":1287154,"title":"","content":"Page 70, in paragraph &quot;Like any Bastet&quot; it reads &quot;and a literal hunger than never goes away&quot; and should be &quot;that&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T20:37:26-08:00","id":1287407,"title":"","content":"Page 85: should be &quot;things man was not meant to know&quot; not mans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T02:30:39-08:00","id":1288214,"title":"","content":"page 121 says &quot;Despite their zany antics, though, tanuki often give good counsel and are among the most reliable guides wilderness travel, especially among the mountains of Japan.&quot; Probably should be guides FOR wilderness travel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T00:35:13-08:00","id":1288541,"title":"","content":"Page 131 - &quot;A scholar of Middle Eastern history would know that in pre-Islamic Persia and Arabia, most people worshipped the djinn and made sacrifices to those spirits as if they were as gods,&quot; should probably drop the last &quot;as&quot;<br /> Page 142: &quot;She's hanging out in the most expected places&quot; should probably be unexpected.<br /> Page 151: in the &quot;Controversy is my Spirit Animal&quot; sidebar, the last paragraph says that a totem is &quot;a greater spirit that shares intimate kindship&quot; which should perhaps be kinship?<br /> Page 167: &quot; Hachiman fears nothing and tends to look down on anything that might be remotely viewed as cowardly Note that this doesn\u2019t mean that he charges in blindly;&quot; probably needs punctuation before &quot;Note&quot;<br /> Page 169: &quot;Some folks capitalize \u201cvodou\u201d out of respect, while others consider such European conventions to be pretentious, simply going a lowercase spelling.&quot; should probably be &quot;going with&quot; or &quot;using&quot;<br /> Page 171: there is a reference to la Baron rather than le baron<br /> Page 200: I know this isn't really what is being asked for, but under Unbelief, it's bizarre to me that something that will literally kill a human in less than 15 minutes (that's assuming a turn is a full minute, which it generally is not, it's 3 seconds to 3 minutes, so this could kill a human in literally under 1 minute.) is described as making the flawed creature &quot;uncomfortable&quot;...perhaps one level of Agg per scene for Painful and per turn for Fatal would be more playable?<br /> Several spots in the charms section references a &quot;Loa background&quot; which, I assume, is identical to Totem but either is not described anywhere or else I just missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25057,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","user":"Janothar","date":". 02-18-2019, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}